# Core Project Rules

# Core Project Rules

* Treat the repository as the primary source of truth.
* Understand existing code before making changes.
* Never assume previous chat history is available.
* Read relevant project documentation before starting significant work.
* Prefer modifying existing functionality over creating duplicate implementations.
* Preserve working behavior unless the task explicitly requires changing it.
* Follow the existing project architecture and conventions.
* Keep changes focused on the requested task.
* Avoid unnecessary refactoring.
* Do not introduce dependencies unless they provide clear value.
* Never invent APIs, configuration, infrastructure, credentials, or project requirements.
* If something is unclear, inspect the repository and configuration before making assumptions.

